    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d11">

                <pb facs="0028" n="16" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg16"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.24/3493/12: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Egypt</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Kirk</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cairo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-05-16T09:00:00+03:00">May 16, 1942—9
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 9:26 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>779. Department’s 410, May 8, midnight, last paragraph. If the Department has not
                    yet selected the representative for civilian supplies on the Middle East Supply
                    Center, General Maxwell suggests that Fred Winant now in the Department is well
                    qualified.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kirk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
